# Grim's Squad Hub — scheduled jobs on the INGESTION box (149.248.39.225).
#
# Install with:  crontab infra/cron/ingestion-box.crontab
# Read with:     crontab -l
#
# ★ THIS BOX OWNS THE SCHEDULED SWEEPS — SQUADRON OWNER, 2026-08-11 ★
#
# The primary serves members: api, web, bot, Postgres, Caddy. This box exists for background work
# and already runs the worker daemon and the EDDN collector. Sweeps belong here, where a slow one
# cannot make a page slow — which is exactly what the second box was stood up to fix, after the
# primary sat at load 6.84 (infra/runbooks/workers-second-box.md).
#
# The primary keeps ONLY the promotion run, because a promotion is a member-facing ceremony that
# posts to Discord and the forum, and it is the one job somebody watches.
#
# ★ THE 03:00 RECONCILE WAS RUNNING TWICE, ON BOTH BOXES ★
#
# It sat in /etc/cron.d/grims-worker here AND in the primary's crontab, so two containers reconciled
# Discord roles against the same database at the same minute every night. Nothing had noticed. It
# lives here now and has been removed from the primary — see infra/cron/root.crontab.
#
# ★ EVERY JOB GOES THROUGH worker-job.sh ★
#
# compose.workers.yml names images `:${GRIMS_IMAGE_TAG:-latest}` exactly as the primary's file does,
# and cron has no such variable in scope. Without the wrapper these ran `:latest` — a tag deploy.sh
# does not move — which is why this box sat on a build from PR #144 while production ran thirteen
# commits ahead. COMPOSE_FILE points the wrapper at this box's stack.

CRON_TZ=UTC
SHELL=/bin/bash
MAILTO=""
COMPOSE_FILE=infra/docker/compose.workers.yml

# Inara profile sweep — pilot ranks for the roster (ADR-004, amended 2026-07-28).
#
# Every 15 minutes is affordable because the adapter batches 30 commanders per request: the whole
# squadron costs about four requests against a budget of 2/minute (INV-033). One name per request
# would have taken ~50 minutes and could only ever have run nightly.
*/15 * * * *   /srv/grims/repo/infra/scripts/worker-job.sh apps/worker/dist/inara-sync.js >> /var/log/grims-inara-sync.log 2>&1

# Discord reconciliation — role drift, orphaned identities, anomalies.
0 3 * * *      /srv/grims/repo/infra/scripts/worker-job.sh apps/worker/dist/main.js >> /var/log/grims-reconcile.log 2>&1

# Commander audit — every commander's squadron and nickname, nightly.
#
# ★ 04:15, NOT 00:15 — deliberately staggered ★
#
# The docs put this at 15 0, the same minute as the promotion run on the primary. Two jobs pulling
# the whole roster at once is avoidable contention, and the audit is the one with no deadline.
15 4 * * *     /srv/grims/repo/infra/scripts/worker-job.sh apps/worker/dist/daily-audit.js >> /var/log/grims-daily-audit.log 2>&1

# ★ role-sync IS NOT HERE, ON PURPOSE — SQUADRON OWNER, 2026-08-11 ★
#
# It is documented as running every minute, which as a cron entry is 1,440 container starts a day,
# each paying Node and Prisma boot to run a handful of indexed queries. The runbook already blames
# container churn for a load incident on the primary.
#
# It runs inside the worker daemon instead — a 60-second tick in a process that is already up, with
# the same job lock every other daemon job uses. See apps/worker/src/daemon.ts.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EMBEDDING — the AI corpus. Every source is useless until it is embedded.
#
# ★ THESE WERE DESTROYED BY INSTALLING THIS FILE — 2026-08-11 ★
#
# `crontab <file>` REPLACES the crontab. This file carried only the sweeps, so
# installing it silently deleted four embedding schedules that had been running
# here since the box was stood up. Nothing failed and nothing said so: the
# knowledge pages went on reporting "Trained within the hour" while the pending
# counts climbed for two days.
#
# They live here now so the file is the whole truth about what this box runs.
# Anything missing from it gets deleted the next time somebody installs it, and
# that is a property of `crontab <file>` nobody can fix — only guard against by
# keeping the file complete.
#
# `grims-embed` is a wrapper at /usr/local/bin, not a worker-job.sh call: it
# predates the wrapper and runs compose.workers.yml directly. It therefore still
# resolves `:latest` rather than the deployed sha — worth correcting, but a
# separate change from restoring what was lost.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*/3 * * * *    /usr/local/bin/grims-embed journal >/dev/null 2>&1
*/5 * * * *    /usr/local/bin/grims-embed forum >/dev/null 2>&1
17 * * * *     /usr/local/bin/grims-embed >/dev/null 2>&1
40 4 * * *     /usr/local/bin/grims-embed inara >/dev/null 2>&1
